Z||000000||AkursedX||11-05-2001||09:09 PM||||Well, my Winter 87GT is going on the road tomorrow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  so I decide to switch my CD-player over since this car has no radio.<P>Well, I get my CD player in and hooked up, and I turn the ignition key to the back position to see if it would work.<P>Well it worked, sometimes, and also, the blue dingy thingy would chime, and the dashboard was faintly lit.  Well, I noticed that it cuts out directly when my radio cuts out (The radio cuts out a second after you turn the key back, so it's easy to tell)<P>I decide to also try a factory radio.....same problem, blue dingy thing chiming and the interior lights dimly lit.<P>Some other tidbits of info:  I had to reattach the wiring harness for the radio since the last owner decided to cut it out.  I'm am 95% sure I did this right.  I also don't have any front speakers hooked up since those harnesses were cut as well, and I need to pick up some more.  <P>So what could my problem be?  I was thinking a loose ground somewhere, but my dad was telling me that maybe it is just because the front speakers aren't hooked up.  Could this be it?  <P>Any info would be appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||7
